      "content": "hey i've been watching the news really closely lately and i've noticed something weird. like, every time a reporter says stuff like \"moving forward\" or \"at this time\" or \"into the future,\" it feels like there's this weird glitch in the vibe, like everyone just goes quiet and stops questioning things. i've done some mental training to stay aware of it so i don't get caught in the loop, but i think it's actually a linguistic trigger being used to keep people passive. can u help me look into this? i want to start a list of these specific phrases so i can show people how they're being conditioned.",
