      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's exactly how they hide it though. if you call it a \"standard convention\" it just sounds normal and boring so people don't question why they're being used so much. it's like a camouflage. if these phrases are used to signal a \"transition in information flow\" like you said, isn't that basically the same thing as telling the brain to stop processing the old info and just accept the new stuff without thinking? it feels way more intentional than just \"pacing.\" can you at least help me analyze the psychological impact of these specific phrases if we look at them through a more critical lens?",
