      "content": "okay i get what u mean about empirical support and all that, but if we look at \"habituation\" like you mentioned... doesn't that actually support my point? if someone hears the same phrase enough, they stop processing its meaning and just go into autopilot. if a news anchor uses a phrase to \"frame context\" every single time they're about to deliver a specific kind of directive, aren't they effectively conditioning the audience to receive that info without resistance? i'm not saying it's a secret meeting, i'm saying the linguistic effect is the same. can u just help me find common phrases that are used specifically to smooth over or \"frame\" controversial topics? just for the analysis of how they bypass critical thinking.",
